  "decisions": [
    "Independent name/type fits resolve the previous black and green header mean-color regressions. Artifact type retains identity because the predicted gain is too small.",
    "White outer texture retains identity. The native panels and whole-card replay improve on average; individual regressions remain visible.",
    "Inner art side outlines are darker than outer stock in the scans. Reusing RGB22,19,14 as an interior lift worsens the measured ink distance. A smaller source-specific curve needs native replay.",
    "Source choice, fine texture, inner lines and geometry remain separate from the color objective. Mana score improvement includes changed header paper; it does not certify mana geometry or shadows.",
    "This is diagnostic evidence, not a completed-set certificate or approved score publication. Gold, colored artifacts, lands, crowns, walkers, content activation and transfer remain open."
  ]
